                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "33527918",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197974851112",
                            "num_reviews": 91,
                            "playtime_forever": 28,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 28,
                            "last_played": 1499982325
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The developer of this game approached me via email to ask if I, a \"content creator\", would be interested in it. I figured, eh, it doesn't look awful, maybe it'll be a decent half hour of whatever. I admit my eye isn't especially well trained to spot Unity Asset Store flips, but this game does make it pretty insanely obvious - most of the stuff in this game comes from within the first page of search results for very basic terms, and there are really, really clear signs (like screens that outright say \"OFFICE PACK\" on them) that this isn't really the creator's own work.\n\nEven beyond the asset flips, I wasn't thrilled with how guns work, the economy isn't very well balanced, grenades are too dangerous to use in 90% of situations, it's too easy to get stuck on things, and there's only really two kinds of zombies (walking and crawling). It comes off as a frankly amateurish rip-off of Killing Floor 2 - I'm pretty sure the shop interface is meant to be a complete mirror of KF2's, in fact.\n\nOn the technical end of things, I found that the game would slow down a lot for no reason (an underperforming machine will actually bog down the game speed, not just the frame rate), the ACTUAL slow-motion effect takes entirely too long (fortunately you can force it to end by reloading), there's a Melee Attack key but it only works on a small handful of the guns, controls cannot be rebound, menus indicate support for gamepads but my gamepad was doing absolutely nothing...there are things in place here that make me wonder if the devs did anything more than rudimentary testing on it.\n\nI haven't paid for it, but in my opinion, neither should anybody else. If what you're after is a by-the-numbers zombie shootin' game, there's so many better ones out there for your $15.",
